ар","a-LAR u-ky-tu-chy-LAR"],["I am happy","мин шат","min shat"],["he is a doctor","ул табиб","ul ta-BIB"],["you all are late","сез соңладыгыз","sez song-la-dy-GYZ"]]},{"id":"singular-and-plural","title":"Singular and plural","text":["The plural ending is -лар / -ләр (or -нар / -нәр after н, м, ң). It depends on the last vowel: китап → китаплар, өй → өйләр. After a number, the noun stays singular: ике китап."],"rows":[["-лар (back vowels)","китап → китаплар","ki-TAP → ki-tap-LAR"],["-ләр (front vowels)","өй → өйләр","euy → euy-LAER"],["after a number","ике китап","i-KE ki-TAP"]],"ex":[["the boy","малай","ma-LAY"],["the girl","кыз","kyz"],["the books","китаплар","ki-tap-LAR"],["a red house","кызыл өй","ky-ZYL euy"],["the cities","шәһәрләр","shae-haer-LAER"],["one cat, two cats","бер мәче, ике мәче","ber maet-CHAE i-KE maet-CHAE"],["one pen, two pens","бер каләм, ике каләм","ber ka-LAEM i-KE ka-LAEM"],["a lesson, lessons","дәрес, дәресләр","daer-ES daer-es-LAER"]]},{"id":"to-be","title":"To be","text":["There is no verb \"to be\" in the present. Add a personal ending to the word: мин студент-мын (I am a student). In the 3rd person there is no ending: ул студент."],"rows":[["I am","-мын / -мен","myn / men"],["you are","-сың / -сең","syng / seng"],["he / she is","(no ending)",""],["we are","-быз / -без","byz / bez"],["they are","(no ending)",""]],"ex":[["I am English","мин инглизмен","min ing-liz-MEN"],["he is a doctor","ул табиб","ul ta-BIB"],["it is Monday","бүген дүшәмбе","byu-GEN dyu-shaem-BE"],["we are from Uzbekistan","без Үзбәкстаннан","bez yuz-baek-stan-NAN"],["they are tall","алар озын","a-LAR o-ZYN"],["I am at home","мин өйдә","min euy-DAE"],["she is tired","ул арыган","ul a-ry-GAN"],["where are you?","сез кайда?","sez kay-DA"],["we are well","без яхшы","bez yakh-SHY"],["the soup is cold","шулпа салкын","shul-PA sal-KYN"]]},{"id":"to-have","title":"Бар / юк: to have","text":["Tatar has no \"to have\". Say \"минем ... бар\" (I have: of me, there is) or \"минем ... юк\" (I do not have). The owner is in the genitive: минем, синең, аның, безнең, сезнең, аларның."],"rows":[["I have","минем ... бар","mi-NEM ... bar"],["you have","синең ... бар","si-NENG ... bar"],["he / she has","аның ... бар","a-NYNG ... bar"],["we have","безнең ... бар","bez-NENG ... bar"],["they have","аларның ... бар","a-lar-NYNG ... bar"]],"ex":[["I have a brother","минем абыем бар","mi-NEM a-by-YEM bar"],["she has two cats","аның ике мәче бар","a-NYNG i-KE maet-CHAE bar"],["we have time","безнең вакыт бар","bez-NENG va-KYT bar"],["I am hungry","мин ашыйсым килә","min a-shy-SYM ki-LAE"],["they have a car","аларның машина бар","a-lar-NYNG ma-SHI-na bar"],["there is a lesson today","бүген дәрес бар","byu-GEN daer-ES bar"],["there is no teacher","укытучы юк","u-ky-tu-CHY yuk"],["I have a question","минем сорау бар","mi-NEM so-RAU bar"]]},{"id":"verbs-present-tense","title":"Verbs: present tense","text":["Take the stem, add -а / -ә (-ый / -и after a vowel), then the personal ending: -м, -сың, (none), -быз, -сыз, -лар. эшлим = I work, эшлисең = you work."],"rows":[["I work","мин эшлим","min esh-LIM"],["you work","син эшлисең","sin esh-li-SENG"],["he / she works","ул эшли","ul esh-LI"],["we work","без эшлибез","bez esh-li-BEZ"],["you (formal) work","сез эшлисез","sez esh-li-SEZ"],["they work","алар эшлиләр","a-LAR esh-li-LAER"]],"ex":[["I drink water","мин су эчәм","min su e-CHAEM"],["he writes a letter","ул хат яза","ul khat ya-ZA"],["we study Tatar","без татар телен өйрәнәбез","bez ta-TAR te-LEN euy-raen-ae-BEZ"],["they play football","алар футбол уйныйлар","a-LAR fut-BOL uyn-yy-LAR"],["she reads a book","ул китап укый","ul ki-TAP u-KYY"],["I know the answer","мин җавапны беләм","min ja-vap-NY be-LAEM"],["you speak English","син инглизчә сөйләшәсең","sin ing-liz-CHAE seu-yae-shae-SENG"],["I live in Tashkent","мин Ташкентта яшим","min tash-KENT-ta ya-SHIM"]]},{"id":"going","title":"Going: бару","text":["The verb бару (to go) is regular. Use the direction ending -га / -гә (to): мәктәпкә барам (I go to school)."],"rows":[["I go","мин барам","min ba-RAM"],["you go","син барасың","sin ba-ra-SYNG"],["he / she goes","ул бара","ul ba-RA"],["we go","без барабыз","bez ba-ra-BYZ"],["they go","алар баралар","a-LAR ba-ra-LAR"]],"ex":[["I am going to school","мин мәктәпкә барам","min maek-taep-KAE ba-RAM"],["where are you going?","син кая барасың?","sin ka-YA ba-ra-SYNG"],["we are going to eat","без ашарга барабыз","bez a-shar-GA ba-ra-BYZ"],["she is going to travel","ул сәяхәткә чыгачак","ul sae-ya-khaet-KAE chy-ga-CHAK"],["let us go!","әйдәгез барыйк!","ae-yda-GEZ ba-RYYK"],["they go home","алар өйгә баралар","a-LAR euy-GAE ba-ra-LAR"],["I go to the market","мин базарга барам","min ba-zar-GA ba-RAM"],["he goes to Kazan","ул Казанга бара","ul ka-zan-GA ba-RA"]]},{"id":"basic-sentences","title":"Basic sentences","text":["The verb comes last. Order: subject, object, verb. The adjective comes before the noun."],"rows":[["subject + object + verb","мин икмәк ашыйм","min ik-MAEK a-SHYM"],["adjective + noun","зур өй","zur euy"],["add time or place","ул бүген монда эшли","ul byu-GEN mon-DA esh-LI"]],"ex":[["I eat bread","мин икмәк ашыйм","min ik-MAEK a-SHYM"],["Maria reads a book","Мария китап укый","ma-RI-ya ki-TAP u-KYY"],["we live in a big house","без зур өйдә яшибез","bez zur euy-DAE ya-shi-BEZ"],["he works here today","ул бүген монда эшли","ul byu-GEN mon-DA esh-LI"],["the dog is black","эт кара","et ka-RA"]]},{"id":"negation","title":"Negation","text":["Add -ма / -мә to the verb stem: эшләмим (I do not work). With nouns and adjectives use \"түгел\" (is not) or \"юк\" (there is none). Always compare with the positive form."],"rows":[["not (verb)","-ма / -мә","ma / mae"],["is not","түгел","tyu-GEL"],["there is none","юк","yuk"],["never","беркайчан да ... -ма","ber-kay-CHAN da"]],"ex":[["I want","мин телим","min te-LIM"],["I do not want","мин теләмим","min te-lae-MIM"],["I speak English","мин инглизчә сөйләшәм","min ing-liz-CHAE seu-yae-SHAEM"],["I do not speak English","мин инглизчә сөйләшмим","min ing-liz-CHAE seu-yaesh-MIM"],["I like it","миңа ошый","mi-NA o-SHYY"],["I do not like it","миңа ошамый","mi-NA o-sha-MYY"],["she is here","ул монда","ul mon-DA"],["she is not here","ул монда түгел","ul mon-DA tyu-GEL"],["I have a car","минем машина бар","mi-NEM ma-SHI-na bar"],["I do not have a car","минем машина юк","mi-NEM ma-SHI-na yuk"],["I understand","мин аңлыйм","min ang-LYM"],["I do not understand","мин аңламыйм","min ang-lam-YM"],["we are tired","без арыдык","bez a-ry-DYK"],["we are not tired","без арымадык","bez a-ry-ma-DYK"],["he works on Sundays","ул якшәмбедә эшли","ul yak-shaem-be-DAE esh-LI"],["he does not work on Sundays","ул якшәмбедә эшләми","ul yak-shaem-be-DAE esh-lae-MI"]]},{"id":"asking-questions","title":"Asking questions","text":["Add the question particle -мы / -ме to the word you are asking about: сез арыгансызмы? (are you tired?). Intonation also works."],"rows":[["statement","ул табиб","ul ta-BIB"],["question","ул табибмы?","ul ta-bib-MY"],["answer yes / no","әйе / юк","ae-YE / yuk"]],"ex":[["do you speak English?","сез инглизчә сөйләшәсезме?","sez ing-liz-CHAE seu-yae-shae-sez-ME"],["is she a doctor?","ул табибмы?","ul ta-bib-MY"],["do you have a pen?","сездә каләм бармы?","sez-DAE ka-LAEM bar-MY"],["are you tired?","сез арыгансызмы?","sez a-ry-gan-sy-ZMY"],["is it far?","ул ерактамы?","ul ye-rak-ta-MY"],["is the restaurant open?","ресторан ачыкмы?","res-to-RAN a-chyk-MY"]]},{"id":"question-words","title":"Question words","text":[],"rows":[["what","нәрсә","naer-SAE"],["who","кем","kem"],["where","кайда","kay-DA"],["when","кайчан","kay-CHAN"],["why","ник","nik"],["how","ничек","ni-CHEK"],["which","кайсы","kay-SY"],["how much / how many","күпме","kyup-ME"]],"ex":[["what is this?","бу нәрсә?","bu naer-SAE"],["who is she?","ул кем?","ul kem"],["where do you live?","сез кайда яшисез?","sez kay-DA ya-shi-SEZ"],["when is the exam?","имтихан кайчан?","im-ti-KHAN kay-CHAN"],["why are you late?","ник соңладыгыз?","nik song-la-dy-GYZ"],["how much is it?","бу күпме тора?","bu kyup-ME to-RA"],["which book?","кайсы китап?","kay-SY ki-TAP"]]},{"id":"possessives","title":"Possessives","text":["Say the owner in the genitive (минем, синең, аның...), then the noun with a possessive ending: минем өем (my house), синең дусларың (your friends)."],"rows":[["my","минем","mi-NEM"],["your","синең","si-NENG"],["his / her","аның","a-NYNG"],["our","безнең","bez-NENG"],["their","аларның","a-lar-NYNG"]],"ex":[["my house","минем өем","mi-NEM eu-YEM"],["your friends","синең дусларың","si-NENG dus-la-RYNG"],["his sister","аның апасы","a-NYNG a-pa-SY"],["our teacher","безнең укытучыбыз","bez-NENG u-ky-tu-chy-BYZ"],["their car","аларның машинасы","a-lar-NYNG ma-shi-na-SY"]]},{"id":"formal-vs-informal","title":"Formal vs informal","text":["Use \"син\" with friends, family and children. Use \"сез\" with strangers, older people and teachers, and add \"-ыз / -егез\" to verbs and nouns."],"rows":[["you (informal)","син","sin"],["you (formal)","сез","sez"],["sir (polite)","әфәнде","ae-faen-DE"]],"ex":[["how are you? (informal)","хәлләр ничек?","khael-LAER ni-CHEK"],["how are you? (formal)","хәлләрегез ничек?","khael-lae-re-GEZ ni-CHEK"],["thank you, sir","рәхмәт, әфәнде","raekh-MAET ae-faen-DE"],["excuse me, madam","гафу итегез, ханым","ga-FU i-te-GEZ kha-NYM"],["please sit down","зинһар, утырыгыз","zin-HAR u-ty-ry-GYZ"]]},{"id":"past-and-future-simple","title":"Past and future (simple)","text":["Past: add -ды / -де (-ты / -те) and the personal ending: эшләдем (I worked). Future: -ачак / -әчәк: эшләячәкмен."],"rows":[["I worked","мин эшләдем","min esh-lae-DEM"],["you worked","син эшләдең","sin esh-lae-DENG"],["he / she worked","ул эшләде","ul esh-lae-DE"],["I will work","мин эшләрмен","min esh-laer-MEN"],["we will work","без эшләрбез","bez esh-laer-BEZ"]],"ex":[["yesterday I worked","кичә мин эшләдем","ki-CHAE min esh-lae-DEM"],["she bought a book","ул китап сатып алды","ul ki-TAP sa-TYP al-DY"],["I will call you tomorrow","мин иртәгә шалтыратырмын","min ir-tae-GAE shal-ty-ra-tyr-MYN"],["we will eat at eight","без сигездә ашарбыз","bez si-gez-DAE a-shar-BYZ"],["they travelled to Spain","алар Испаниягә сәяхәт иттеләр","a-LAR is-pa-ni-ya-GAE sae-ya-KHAET it-te-LAER"],["I went to the market","мин базарга бардым","min ba-zar-GA bar-DYM"],["he will come later","ул соңрак килер","ul song-RAK ki-LER"]]},{"id":"commands","title":"Commands","text":["Informal: use the verb stem (кил! = come!). Make it negative with -ма / -мә (килмә! = do not come!). Formal: add -ыгыз / -егез (килегез!)."],"rows":[["come! (informal)","кил!","kil"],["do not come!","килмә!","kil-MAE"],["come! (formal)","килегез!","ki-le-GEZ"]],"ex":[["come here","монда кил","mon-DA kil"],["do not come here","монда килмә","mon-DA kil-MAE"],["sit down","утыр","u-TYR"],["do not sit down","утырма","u-tyr-MA"],["be quiet","тын бул","tyn bul"],["do not be late","соңлама","song-la-MA"],["open the door","ишекне ач","i-shek-NE ach"],["close the window","тәрәзәне яп","tae-rae-zae-NE yap"],["listen to me","мине тыңла","mi-NE tyng-LA"],["do not worry","борчылма","bor-chyl-MA"],["speak slowly","әкрен сөйлә","ae-KREN seu-y-LAE"],["wait a moment","бер минут көт","ber mi-NUT keut"]]},{"id":"can-must-want","title":"Can, must, want","text":["Can: verb + -а ала (мин йөзә алам). Must: \"кирәк\" or \"тиеш\". Want: \"теләү\" or \"-ыйсым килә\". Forbidden: \"ярамый\"."],"rows":[["I can","мин ... а алам","min ... a-LAM"],["I must","миңа ... кирәк","mi-NA ... ki-RAEK"],["I want","мин ... телим","min ... te-LIM"]],"ex":[["I can swim","мин йөзә алам","min yeu-ZAE a-LAM"],["I cannot swim","мин йөзә алмыйм","min yeu-ZAE al-MYM"],["can you help me?","миңа булыша аласызмы?","mi-NA bu-ly-SHA a-la-sy-ZMY"],["we must go","безгә барырга кирәк","bez-GAE ba-ryr-GA ki-RAEK"],["we must not go","безгә бару ярамый","bez-GAE ba-RU ya-ra-MYY"],["I want to eat","мин ашарга телим","min a-shar-GA te-LIM"],["I do not want to eat","мин ашарга теләмим","min a-shar-GA te-lae-MIM"],["you can come","син килә аласың","sin ki-LAE a-la-SYNG"],["you cannot come","син килә алмыйсың","sin ki-LAE al-my-SYNG"],["she wants to study","ул укырга тели","ul u-kyr-GA te-LI"],["I must work today","бүген миңа эшләргә кирәк","byu-GEN mi-NA esh-laer-GAE ki-RAEK"],["you must not run","сиңа йөгерергә ярамый","si-NA yeu-ge-rer-GAE ya-ra-MYY"]]},{"id":"in-on-at","title":"In, on, at","text":["Tatar uses endings, not prepositions: -да / -дә = in / at; -га / -гә = to; -дан / -дән = from. \"Өстендә\" = on, \"астында\" = under, \"янында\" = next to."],"rows":[["in / at","-да / -дә","da / dae"],["to","-га / -гә","ga / gae"],["on","өстендә","eus-ten-DAE"],["under","астында","as-tyn-DA"],["next to","янында","yan-yn-DA"]],"ex":[["the book is on the table","китап өстәл өстендә","ki-TAP eus-TAEL eus-ten-DAE"],["the cat is under the table","мәче өстәл астында","maet-CHAE eus-TAEL as-tyn-DA"],["I am at school","мин мәктәптә","min maek-taep-TAE"],["I am at home","мин өйдә","min euy-DAE"],["the shop is next to the bank","кибет банк янында","ki-BET bank yan-yn-DA"],["the park is near the station","парк вокзалга якын","park vok-zal-GA ya-KYN"],["we meet in the morning","без иртән очрашабыз","bez ir-TAEN och-ra-sha-BYZ"],["the lesson is at nine","дәрес тугызда","daer-ES tu-gyz-DA"],["the key is in the bag","ачкыч сумкада","ach-KYCH sum-ka-DA"]]},{"id":"comparing-things","title":"Comparing things","text":["Add -рак / -рәк for \"more\": зуррак (bigger). \"Иң\" = the most: иң зур. \"-дан\" = than: теге-дән яхшырак."],"rows":[["bigger than","...дан зуррак","dan zur-RAK"],["better","яхшырак","yakh-shy-RAK"],["the biggest","иң зур","ing zur"]],"ex":[["big, bigger, the biggest","зур, зуррак, иң зур","zur, zur-RAK, ing zur"],["small, smaller, the smallest","кечкенә, кечкенәрәк, иң кечкенә","kech-ke-NAE, kech-ke-nae-RAEK, ing kech-ke-NAE"],["this is better than that","бу тегедән яхшырак","bu te-ge-DAEN yakh-shy-RAK"],["this is worse than that","бу тегедән начаррак","bu te-ge-DAEN na-char-RAK"],["she is taller than me","ул миннән озынрак","ul min-NAEN o-zyn-RAK"],["Tashkent is bigger than Samarkand","Ташкент Самаркандтан зуррак","tash-KENT sa-mar-kand-TAN zur-RAK"],["it is the cheapest","бу иң арзан","bu ing ar-ZAN"],["the same as","шундый ук","shun-DYY uk"]]},{"id":"everyday-sentences","title":"Everyday sentences","text":["Extra practice with the most useful patterns."],"rows":[],"ex":[["he is a teacher","ул укытучы","ul u-ky-tu-CHY"],["you (plural) are students","сез укучылар","sez u-ku-chy-LAR"],["I am happy","мин шат","min shat"],["she is at school","ул мәктәптә","ul maek-taep-TAE"],["you are my friend","син минем дусым","sin mi-NEM du-SYM"],["it is cold","салкын","sal-KYN"],["I study English","мин инглиз телен өйрәнәм","min ing-LIZ te-LEN euy-raen-AEM"],["he teaches maths","ул математика укыта","ul ma-te-MA-ti-ka u-ky-TA"],["they work every day","алар көн саен эшлиләр","a-LAR keun sa-EN esh-li-LAER"],["is this your book?","бу синең китабыңмы?","bu si-NENG ki-ta-byng-MY"],["are they here?","алар монданмы?","a-LAR mon-dan-MY"],["do you like tea?","син чәйне яратасыңмы?","sin chaey-NE ya-ra-ta-syng-MY"],["what time is it?","сәгать ничә?","sae-GAT ni-CHAE"],["whose book is this?","бу кемнең китабы?","bu kem-NENG ki-ta-BY"],["how old are you?","сезгә ничә яшь?","sez-GAE ni-CHAE yash"],["how do you say it?","аны ничек әйтәләр?","a-NY ni-CHEK ae-tae-LAER"],["your book (formal)","сезнең китабыгыз","sez-NENG ki-ta-by-GYZ"],["their house","аларның өйләре","a-lar-NYNG euy-lae-RE"],["my phone","минем телефоным","mi-NEM te-le-fo-NYM"],["excuse me, sir","гафу итегез, әфәнде","ga-FU i-te-GEZ ae-faen-DE"],["please sit down (formal)","зинһар, утырыгыз","zin-HAR u-ty-ry-GYZ"],["come here (informal)","монда кил","mon-DA kil"],["yesterday I was tired","кичә мин арыган идем","ki-CHAE min a-ry-GAN i-DEM"],["I will study tomorrow","мин иртәгә укырмын","min ir-tae-GAE u-kyr-MYN"],["we went to the park","без паркка бардык","